.SH NAME
ssoossh-ca - Print the CA public key of the configured ssoossh server.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBssoossh ca [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the public key of the server's certificate authority in authorized_keys format, one key per line (two while a CA rotation is under way). Hosts that accept ssoossh certificates name this file in sshd's TrustedUserCAKeys.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for ca


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	path to an extra config file, merged after the standard locations

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	server address, e.g. https://ssh.example.com; https is assumed when no scheme is given

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	trace what the command is doing, to stderr; repeat for more (-v steps, -vv requests and files, -vvv bodies)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Trust ssoossh certificates on an sshd host
  ssoossh ca | sudo tee /etc/ssh/ssoossh_ca.pub
  # then, in sshd_config: TrustedUserCAKeys /etc/ssh/ssoossh_ca.pub
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBssoossh(1)\fP


